## What was carried over

The substance of the upstream plugin is Korean prose: two output-style guidance
documents under `plugins/fluent-korean/output-styles/`. Those two documents are
reproduced in this package, byte-identical to their upstream counterparts except
for the YAML front-matter at the top of each file. The Korean text was **not**
translated, edited, summarised, or reworded. That is deliberate — it is the
product, and a translation of it would defeat its purpose.

Because that prose is a substantial portion of the upstream work, it is
redistributed under the upstream MIT License, and the original copyright notice
is retained verbatim in the `LICENSE` file in this package. The MIT License
requires that the copyright notice and permission notice travel with all copies
and substantial portions; they do.

## What this package adds

Everything that is not upstream Korean prose — the DSH plugin entry point, the
configuration schema, the Settings surface, the README files, and this NOTICE —
is original work for this port. It is distributed under the same MIT License,
whose text is reproduced at the bottom of `LICENSE`.

## Style differences

The upstream documents carry a Claude Code-specific front-matter key,
`keep-coding-instructions`, which controls whether Claude Code's built-in coding
instructions are dropped. DSH has no equivalent mechanism, and this port does
not attempt to fake one. See the "Known limitation" section of `README.md` for
what that means in practice. This port does not modify the prose to compensate;
it changes only the front-matter.

